 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? They' probably still warm, so you could cook them in a big pan with some stock and cover it. Then put the pan in a sink of cold water, it' cool faster. Then add a splash of lemon or a bit of vinegar. It helps, but really you want to eat them soon after. Cooked and cold steaks taste flat. Tougher than most, probably. He probably just wants them as warm as possible. Then you can put the rest in the fridge tonight and have them warmed up for him tomorrow.",
